course: dictionary
lesson: 7741
title: Pumice: a rock that floats
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Lava full of gas bubbles can cool quickly into rock with many small holes, such as pumice.» Lava, cool and rock tell you that pumice is a kind of rock.
explain: Pumice is a very light, rough grey rock full of tiny holes. It forms when frothy lava from a volcano cools quickly. «Pumice is a volcanic rock so full of gas bubbles that it can float on water.» The gas bubbles are why it floats, which is a surprising thing for a rock to do.
explain: The second meaning is about feet and bathrooms: a pumice stone is a piece of this rock, used to rub away hard skin. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence is about rubbing hard skin off your feet, then pumice stone must mean the rock piece you rub with, and it still makes sense.
fact: Pumice is an uncountable noun, so you say some pumice, not a pumice. A single piece is a pumice stone.
fact: Pumice is an igneous rock, made from volcanic lava that cools.
fact: «Pumice» means a very light, rough grey rock full of tiny holes.
fact: Pumice can float on water because of the gas bubbles inside it.
fact: After some eruptions, rafts of floating pumice drift on the sea.
exercise: «Lava full of gas bubbles can cool quickly into rock with many small holes, such as pumice.» What is pumice? | A metal used to build bridges | A kind of bread baked near volcanoes | *A light rock full of tiny holes, made from cooled lava | A bird that lives by the sea
exercise: What is a pumice stone used for? | To keep a door shut | To make bath water warm | *To rub away hard skin, for example on your feet | To catch fish in a river
exercise: «Pumice is a volcanic rock so full of gas bubbles that it can float on water.» Find and copy the word that tells you where pumice comes from. | water | sea | bubbles | *volcanic
test: «Pumice is a volcanic rock so full of gas bubbles that it can float on water.» Why can pumice float? | Because it is made of metal | *Because it is full of gas bubbles | Because it is wrapped in plastic | Because it is very heavy
test: «After some eruptions, rafts of floating pumice drift on the sea.» What are the rafts made of? | Seaweed and sand | Ice from the poles | *Floating pumice rock | Wood from old ships
exam: Which sentence uses pumice to mean a piece of rock used on feet? | Pumice is a loud noise | The pumice lives in the forest | *Use a pumice stone to rub the hard skin on your heels | Pumice is a famous footballer
